BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:After School Club: Robots Sensors Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T173000
UID:6ab57389ca248a0029183043@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore how robots use sensors and programming to interact wit
 h their environment using Scribbler Robots. Learn how NASA uses robots to 
 explore Mars\, then gain hands-on experience testing robots and discover h
 ow programming can connect them with non-intended devices.\nFor children a
 ges 6-12. Drop in to capacity.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Room A\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab57389ca248a0029183043
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library:  Milkweed Ornament
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T160000
UID:6a88d0d357c264087ad2d3a3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Part 4 of a series of workshops for children and adults\, expl
 oring local flora through embroidery and felt collage. This event is part
  of the\nArtists in the Library\nprogram\, hosted by Artist\, Sarah Zanche
 tta.\nAll ages\nprogram\; children ages 6 to 14 must be accompanied by a p
 arent or caregiver.  Registration is required. Space is limited.\nNote:\nE
 ach workshop requires separate registration. Registered participant spaces
  are held for 15 minutes after which drop-ins are allowed\nMeet the Reside
 nt:\nSarah Zanchetta (she/they) is a queer textile artist and educator who
 se practice dives into the loss of connection and knowledge of poisonous p
 lants in North America. Zanchetta uses textiles\, texts\, and hosts commun
 ity workshops to create intimate works and spaces where we can unfold our 
 curiosities\, care and anxieties about what grows beside our feet. She ho
 lds a Master of Visual Studies from the University of Toronto (2023) and a
  BFA from OCAD University (2018).\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Lower Level\, Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a88d0d357c264087ad2d3a3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
