DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T150000
UID:6aa18cb9a5dbde002aa2ffa0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Make your own custom creation out of beads and watch as they g
 et ironed together into a 2D object .\nAges 4 - 17\nThe program will take 
 place in the Auditorium located in the basement. Elevator on site. If you 
 have any questions\, please call Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910.\nInformat
 ion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answ
 erline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bendale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa18cb9a5dbde002aa2ffa0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:After School Animation with Piskel
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T170000
UID:6ac64be029c3d600332e3bb6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Piskel can be used to create game sprites (i.e.\, 2D images ov
 erlaid onto a scene)\, animations\, pixel-art for social media\, etc. This
  software gives you the ability to paint and erase pixels\, resize pixel a
 rt to a bigger scale\, create animation sheets for games\, and more.\nSpac
 e is limited. Bring a USB stick if you'd like to save your work.
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac64be029c3d600332e3bb6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STEAM Workshop: Disc Launcher
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T150000
UID:6ac64e17de300e004518ce03@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, children will design and build a complex st
 ructure\, the disc launcher.  They will create a motorized mini disk launc
 her. Load it up and watch the disks spin and fly. Test it out with your fr
 iends to see who’s disk flies the furthest.\nProjects are designed to st
 rengthen problem-solving\, creativity\, and collaboration skills in a fun\
 , hands-on environment.\nThis program is for children ages 9 to 12.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac64e17de300e004518ce03
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
