UID:6a9b0386be148200298c8293@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For children ages 6-8 years with their parents or caregivers.\
 n(Re)discover the joy of reading in this relaxed family program for kids 6
 -8 and their parents or caregivers. Each week\, explore a new story or the
  next chapter of a favourite book together. Then\, head on your own readin
 g adventures and enjoy independent reading and playful story remixing with
  family and friends.\nRegistration is required. Registration opens online 
 on Friday\, September 11 at 9 am. Space is limited.\nLive or automated clo
 sed captioning\, sign language interpretation\, or attendant services are 
 available upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in adv
 ance to: tpl.ca/accessibility-events.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-
 5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b0386be148200298c8293
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
