BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Halloween 3D Craft Part 1 & Part 2
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T190000
UID:6abac1e09dbc2b002c8ad59c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this program\, kids will create a custom Halloween-themed p
 rop. In part 1\, we will learn how to create the prop using the 3D design 
 website Tinkercad. In part 2\, children will decorate their 3D-printed des
 ign with various supplies.\nFor children ages 8-12. Register online.\n*Ple
 ase only register if you can attend both sessions.\nPart 1: Tuesday Octobe
 r 20 @ 6-7:30PM\nPart 2: Tuesday October 27 @ 6-7PM\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the\nPublic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
 )\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for\nevent and program re
 gistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library\nhan
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tp
 l.ca\, 416-397-\n5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Scarborough Civic Centre\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abac1e09dbc2b002c8ad59c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to 3D Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T183000
UID:6aad8a09f5c6780c7049238b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how 3D printers work and how you can print at the Toront
 o Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs. This class includes hands-on
  instruction with Prusa Slicer\, the software used to prepare your 3D obje
 ct file for printing on a Prusa MK3S+ 3D printer.\nNote: Customers are no 
 longer required to attend a mandatory 3D printing class prior to using a 3
 D printer at the Toronto Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs. This 
 class is for those who are interested in learning more about 3D printing a
 nd how to use the Prusa software.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Digital Innovation Hub\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad8a09f5c6780c7049238b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:40th Anniversary of Franklin in the Dark
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T235959
UID:6a89c44b29a7dd0d6745c19b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:First published in 1986\, join us in celebrating 40 years of t
 he beloved Canadian turtle\, Franklin. Discover the series’ original dra
 fts by author Paulette Bourgeois and illustrator Brenda Clark\, alongside 
 other terrific turtle tales! Visit the Osborne Collection to experience ou
 r exhibit.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, 4th Floor- Osborne Collection
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a89c44b29a7dd0d6745c19b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
