BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DIY Solar-Powered Fan Kit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T150000
UID:6ac823bb377296003a4aaf35@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:DIY Solar-Powered Fan Kit\nCytron DIY Solar-Powered Fan Kit\nE
 ducational DIY Solar-Powered Fan Kit\nSuitable for children aged 5 years a
 nd above\nProvides learning about renewable energy\nIncludes all component
 s for easy assembly\nThe\nCytron DIY Solar-Powered Fan Kit\nprovides an en
 gaging and interactive way for children to learn about renewable energy so
 urces. The fan\, which is powered by a solar panel\, is simple enough to b
 e assembled by a 5-year-old with the assistance of an adult. Children who 
 are 5 years old and above can independently assemble it.\nThe primary obje
 ctive of this kit is to facilitate a better understanding of how solar pan
 els and electric motors function. The kit is comprehensive\, providing all
  the necessary components for the assembly of the fan. These include woode
 n parts for the fan structure\, a compact solar panel\, a small DC motor\,
  a propeller\, double-sided tape\, and cable ties.\nRegistration Begins  o
 n October 26th 2026 at 10:00 A.M. Spaces are limited this program will tak
 e place again in December.\nThe program will take place in the Auditorium 
 located in the basement. Elevator on site. If you have any questions\, ple
 ase call Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910.\nInformation Collection Notice:\n
 The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public L
 ibrary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d)
 . The information will only be used for event and program registration\, d
 elivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your infor
 mation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-3
 97-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bendale\, The program will take place in the Auditorium located i
 n the basement. Elevator on site. If you have any questions\, please call 
 Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac823bb377296003a4aaf35
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DIY Solar Powered Wooden Car STEM Kit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T150000
UID:6ac82201a85a2c00337e2ff9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:DIY Solar Powered Wooden Car STEM Kit\nDo It Yourself Solar Po
 wered Wooden Car STEM Kit\nTeaches about renewable energy and solar power\
 nSimple and yet educational\nNo soldering is needed\, moveable car\nAge: 5
 +\nIt's time to make your own toy! Better yet\, a solar-powered wooden car
 ! Get the\nDIY Solar Powered Wooden Car STEM Kit\nto keep your kids occupi
 ed with hands-on activities while enjoying the "robot" moving around that 
 is powered by green energy\, renewable energy - Solar Power.\nThe Registra
 tion open's up on October 26th 2026 at 10:00 a.m. spaces are limited and t
 his program will take place again in December\nThe program will take plac
 e in the Auditorium located in the basement. Elevator on site. If you have
  any questions\, please call Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bendale\, The program will take place in the Auditorium located i
 n the basement. Elevator on site. If you have any questions\, please call 
 Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac82201a85a2c00337e2ff9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DIY Wooden Pneumatic Horse Kit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T170000
UID:6ac81fba377296003a4aae21@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:DIY Wooden Pneumatic Horse\nDIY Wooden Pneumatic Horse Kit  t
 eaches principles of air pressure and pneumatics to kids Ages 6 and up. Ea
 ch child will get to take home one kit they build.\nDIY Wooden Pneumatic H
 orse Kit\nEngages children in practical activities\nTeaches principles of 
 air pressure and pneumatics\nIncludes all components for easy assembly\nAg
 e: 5+\nThe\nDIY Wooden Pneumatic Horse Kit\nis an engaging and educational
  assembly kit designed specifically for children between the ages of 5 to 
 12. This kit offers children the opportunity to participate in practical a
 ctivities\, while simultaneously observing the movement of a wooden horse\
 , propelled by the simple push and pull of a syringe. This action illustra
 tes the principles of air pressure and pneumatic systems in a fun and inte
 ractive way.\nThe kit includes all necessary components for the assembly o
 f a pneumatic horse\, such as pre-cut wooden pieces for the horse structur
 e\, a pair of syringes of different sizes\, orange rubber rings that funct
 ion as grippers\, self-tapping screws\, metal shafts of varying lengths\, 
 a small screwdriver\, and a plastic tube. The assembly process does not re
 quire any soldering.\nRegistration Begins  on October 26th 2026 at 10:00 
 A.M. Spaces are limited this program will take place again in December.\nT
 he program will take place in the Auditorium located in the basement. Elev
 ator on site. If you have any questions\, please call Bendale Branch at 41
 6-396-8910.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bendale\, The program will take place in the Auditorium located i
 n the basement. Elevator on site. If you have any questions\, please call 
 Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac81fba377296003a4aae21
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
