BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Let's Make a Graphic Novel! Workshop with Tory Woollcott
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T170000
UID:6aa18e6aa5dbde002aa30000@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Led by the professional cartoonist\, Tory Woollcott\, this wo
 rkshop teaches the fundamentals of story outlining and narrative structure
  as it applies to comics & graphic novels\, prose\, or even video games! D
 rop in\, limited spots.\nTory Woollcott is a Toronto-based author\, illust
 rator\, designer\, and educator whose work spans graphic novels\, science 
 comics\, audio dramas\, podcasts\, and kids' books. She is the author of S
 cience Comics: The Brain: The Ultimate Thinking Machine (First Second Book
 s)\, a vibrant and accessible exploration of neuroscience\, illustrated by
  Alex Graudins. Her debut graphic novel\, Mirror Mind\, is a celebrated a
 utobiography that recounts her experiences growing up with dyslexia. Other
  notable works include the audio drama Awake with Sparklermonthly\, the tr
 avel diary Toronto to Tuscany (created in collaboration with Kean Soo)\, a
 nd two successful Kickstarter campaigns: the Tessera Oracle and its follow
 -up\, the Trine Oracle.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa18e6aa5dbde002aa30000
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
