DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T170000
UID:6a90c28caafa6100295fad2d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun! For ages 6-12. Program supplies are all provided.\nSnacks are offere
 d during the After School Club for participants. Ingredient lists will be 
 available. Snacks are generously supported\, in part\, by donors.\nMonday 
 October 5: Snap Circuits\n- Learn the basics of circuitry and explore the 
 many fun things you can make using a Snap Circuit kit!\nMonday October 12:
  CLOSED FOR THANKSGIVING\nMonday October 19: Iron-On Patch Pouches\n- Deco
 rate a canvas pouch of pencil case with fun iron-on patches!\nMonday Octob
 er 26: Mask Making\n- Get creative and paint your own paper mask!\nAccessi
 bility\nLive or automated closed captioning\, sign language interpretation
 \, intervenor services\, or attendant services are available upon request.
  Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to:\ntpl.ca/access
 ibility-events\n.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Program Room - Basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90c28caafa6100295fad2d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
