SUMMARY:Family Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T160000
UID:6a974ba51c197d11325c810a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all kids ages 9-12 and their parents\, or caregivers!\
 nLooking for a fun way to spend time together? Join our Monthly Family Boo
 k Club!\nEach month\, you will read a different book. Share thoughts\, ide
 as and favorite moments. Connect with other families through discussions a
 nd activities.\nRegistration online. Please register ONCE for your pair (c
 hild and caregiver).\n✨ This month’s featured book:\nThe BFG by Roald 
 Dahl!\n✨
LOCATION:Queen/Saulter
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a974ba51c197d11325c810a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:After School Club: Diorama Art with Soyeon Kim
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T170000
UID:6a91b84f1c197d11325b77f5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how artist/illustrator Soyeon Kim brings a world to life
  in her diorama art. Learn about this amazing art form and how you can sta
 rt making your own diorama at home. Soyeon will share how she uses drawing
 \, colouring\, and cutting techniques to assemble layered scenes that show
  depth\, texture\, and imagination. Then provide some inspiration for anyo
 ne ready to create their own world!\nRecommended materials:\nrecycled card
 board box\, white paper (letter size)\, drawing tools (pencil\, eraser)\
 , colouring tools\, scissors\, glue stick\, tape\nZoom URL to access t
 he online program will be emailed to registrants ahead of program date.\nT
 his online program is suitable for children ages 6-12. Younger children ma
 y require assistance from caregivers. It is recommended that parents or ca
 regivers are present during this live program. Questions about online prog
 rams? Please email us at programproposals@tpl.ca.\nInformation Collection 
 Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto
  Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, 
 and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registr
 ation\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles y
 our information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\
 n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a91b84f1c197d11325b77f5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
